.claude/plans/PLAN-193/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-4.txt:13:- **P2 — Output-parent symlinks are followed.** [`.claude/scripts/re-pin-codex.py:1814`](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc1.jJzf7b/wt/.claude/scripts/re-pin-codex.py:1814). With a valid plan document and its `PLAN-NNN/` directory symlinked outside the checkout, ordinary generation follows that parent and creates the pack externally. Only the output leaf is checked for existence; `is_dir()` accepts symlinked parents. Existing files remain protected, limiting the damage. **Minimal fix:** reject symlink components beneath the resolved repository root and perform publication through a validated parent directory.
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r2/verdict-rc1-3.txt:16:   [`.claude/scripts/mutant_sandbox.py:133`](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc1.3JOeTU/wt/.claude/scripts/mutant_sandbox.py:133), [cleanup at :147](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc1.3JOeTU/wt/.claude/scripts/mutant_sandbox.py:147). When a test command launches workers, `subprocess.run(timeout=…)` kills its direct child without terminating the descendants. A read-only process probe reproduced a surviving descendant after timeout. The helper then removes the worktree beneath those processes; repeated retries can accumulate workers and interfere with subsequent verification.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-rc1-20260918-NOGO-r2/verdict-rc1-3.txt:25:Validation used Python 3.9.6, source inspection, in-memory fault probes, and a read-only subprocess probe. The checkout remains unchanged; no complete upgrade or live Workflow smoke test ran.
.claude/plans/PLAN-192/repass-ga/verdict-ga-2.txt:5:- **Registration — conditions 2/3:** The added registrations in `templates/settings/settings.base.json:228` and `templates/settings/settings.user.json:325` retain blocking behavior. Executing the actual upgrade merge against both v1.4.0 profiles added exactly two Workflow registrations, preserved supplied adopter settings, and was idempotent. All three fresh-install stack merges retained both hooks.
